@Ekaterina Galetski - Can you tell me a little bit more about this piece of info - "Reliable site"? I'm looking at the extension and I'm not seeing where or how that's used. 

I think for 'big name' sites like Amazon, Home Depot, etc., this piece of info might not be necessary. 

Might be more appropriate for smaller, unknown sellers. Wdyt?

@Ekaterina Galetski - Hey Kate - Drafted some copy for your new proposed callouts.  

As for image or no image for this particular callout - if the user has not changed their default settings, the RC panel will automatically open the next PDP the user visits.

I get that it's important for the user to know how to get back to RC. But also - the way the default experience for this feature is designed, the browser does the work of opening RC when we think it's relevant. So, the user likely doesn't HAVE to know this in order to get value from RC.

@Ekaterina Galetski answering your questions here:
1. I think we may not need to announce anything specific but to state that the Review Checker is now part of the sidebar - since we have had the sidebar available on the left for some time now and it's a known pattern to have the sidebars on the left (for assistive technology users this is, in this case, before the web content instead of after it).
2. (ideally, we'd update the messaging to not to use the spacial navigation altogether; re-messaging or not would not be an a11y team call)

